# Diagnostic reports
# PATCHED (audit fix): this used to be a blanket `*.json` rule with only
# two path exceptions (!frontend/tsconfig.json, !realdiag-demo/**/*.json).
# That meant ANY new JSON file added anywhere in the repo - a new data
# file under backend/data/, a lockfile, a config file - would be silently
# untracked unless whoever added it knew to `git add -f` it. The CI
# workflow even has a comment acknowledging uncertainty about whether
# package-lock.json is tracked, which traces back to this rule. Scoped
# down to the actual ad-hoc report files this was meant to ignore.
reports/
diagnostic_report*.json
system_diagnostic*.json
*.csv
frontend/out/
backups/
